  {
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "I believe I know _why_ this happened, need to have some talks internally about what we can do to resolve this in future.\n\nWe package 7.0 headers and libs in the pytorch-triton-rocm build, which seems to set TRITON_HIP_DRIVER_REQ_MAJOR_VERSION to 7 - https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/blob/main/third_party/amd/backend/driver.c#L36C46-L36C63\n\nThen we hit the runtime error here https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/blob/main/third_party/amd/backend/driver.c#L90\n\nIn order to resolve this going forward we will likely need to start build triton wheel for latest N and N-1 version of ROCm, but considering 7.1 is now out now we need to have a chat about what to do with 6.4 here. \n\nWill report back on issue as updates come in.\n",
    "created_at": "2025-11-11T11:15:24Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/167411#issuecomment-3516364126",
